      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "WANG Ch'ing-yün 王慶雲 (T. 家鐶, 賢關, H. 樂一, 雁汀), Apr. 14, 1798–1862, Apr. 6, official and scholar, was a native of Min-hsien (Foochow). His family settled at Foochow in the sixteenth century and came to be known as the Hsi-ch'ing Wang-shih 西清王氏.",
